# Crystal-orbital diagrams and hybridization (crystod --diagram / --atomic-orbital);
# testsuite section 3
# The crystal orbital diagram (COD): the two fragment sublattices (--co-left/--co-right, full-electron
# basis from the archived PySCF atomic levels in reference/ + point-charge ligand field of the removed
# sublattice) are the pre-bonding states; states sharing a little-group irrep at k mix into bonding/antibonding.

crystod --atomic-orbital Sc_d F_p -c 221_PPOSCAR_ScF3


# Derive the crystal orbital diagram of BaTiO3 by calculating the energy levels of 
# BaTiO3, sublattices (BaTi)6+ and (O3)6- by using B3LYP hybrid functional 
crystod --diagram -c 99_PPOSCAR_BaTiO3 --pyscf --co-left BaTi --co-right O3 --ke-cutoff 150 --kmesh 2 2 2 --max-l 2 --xc b3lyp --chk BaTiO3_b3lyp.chk


# Derive the crystal orbital diagram of ScF3 by calculating the energy levels of
# ScF3, sublattices Sc3+ and (F3)3- by using PBE functional
crystod --diagram -c 221_PPOSCAR_ScF3 --pyscf --co-left Sc --co-right F3 --ke-cutoff 80 --kmesh 2 2 2 --max-l 2 --xc pbe --chk ScF3.chk


# Derive the crystal orbital diagram of BaTiO3 by calculating the energy levels of
# SrTiO3, sublattices (SrTi)6+ and (O3)6- by using B3LYP hybrid functional without using ghost atoms
crystod --diagram -c 221_PPOSCAR_SrTiO3 --pyscf --co-left SrTi --co-right O3 --ke-cutoff 150 --kmesh 2 2 2 --max-l 2 --xc b3lyp --no-ghost --chk SrTiO3_b3lyp.chk


# The command below is removed:
crystod --diagram -c 221_PPOSCAR_ScF3 --co-left Sc --co-right F3 --atomic-orbital Sc-3d F-2p


